WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:08.884
A secret agent must be solitary and austere.

00:00:09.265 --> 00:00:10.125
No affections,

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:11.766
no ties,

00:00:12.987 --> 00:00:14.326
no sentimentalities.

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:18.148
Said a man who should know.

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:20.730
Richard Saga,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.211
Stalin's master spy in Tokyo.

00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:27.257
Sorga himself didn't follow those rules at all.

00:00:28.077 --> 00:00:29.219
He was an eccentric,

00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:30.858
loved women and alcohol,

00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:33.060
and was known for his escapades.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.442
Perhaps the most ingenious of all disguises,

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:39.984
he is considered one of the great masters of his trade.

00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:46.608
He was opposed to war and believed that he could help to avoid it by doing his work.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:53.031
He really was one of those people who is highly motivated by his ideology.

00:00:55.073 --> 00:00:57.634
Saga is considered to be the master spy of the

00:00:57.974 --> 00:00:58.474
20th century,

00:00:58.754 --> 00:01:00.076
not just by the Soviet Union,

00:01:00.315 --> 00:01:01.696
but by the USA as well.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.822
He must have been a fascinating person.

00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.123
If I had been a woman in his time,

00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:14.626
I might have hopelessly fallen for him too.

00:01:20.129 --> 00:01:20.909
Richard Saga.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.331
Stalin's James Bond.

00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:30.662
The betrayal of a master spy.

00:01:38.368 --> 00:01:39.590
What would have happened if...

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.731
If Stauffenberg's plot had succeeded,

00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:44.974
if Pearl Harbor hadn't taken place,

00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:46.556
and if shortly before that,

00:01:46.695 --> 00:01:47.516
Richard Sorge,

00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:48.938
a spy with conviction,

00:01:49.078 --> 00:01:51.520
hadn't fallen into the clutches of the Japanese?

00:01:56.703 --> 00:01:57.864
At that point in time,

00:01:57.944 --> 00:01:59.626
Hitler had conquered half of Europe.

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:03.629
The Japanese Empire was undertaking a similar march across Asia,

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:07.012
their incursions leaving nothing but piles of rubble in their wake.

00:02:08.853 --> 00:02:09.274
Together,

00:02:09.353 --> 00:02:13.576
Nazi Germany and Japan want to wipe out the enemy of all humankind,

00:02:13.736 --> 00:02:14.418
communism,

00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:17.000
so they join forces against the Soviet Union.

00:02:22.463 --> 00:02:27.128
self-proclaimed master race lines up to stomp out communism once and for all.

00:02:33.995 --> 00:02:35.175
Operating out of Tokyo,

00:02:35.376 --> 00:02:40.901
the committed communist Sorga completes his mission and betrays the German Reich to the Soviet Union,

00:02:41.663 --> 00:02:43.024
one dictator to another.

00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:54.198
Shortly before his spy ring gets busted,

00:02:54.498 --> 00:02:59.582
Sorge sends a message that proves decisive for the further course of the Russian military campaign.

00:03:00.003 --> 00:03:03.926
The seemingly invincible German armed forces get their first scratches.

00:03:08.449 --> 00:03:11.192
By the time the tide turns in favor of the Soviets,

00:03:11.512 --> 00:03:13.794
Sorge's era had already come to an end.

00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:17.997
Dr.

00:03:18.076 --> 00:03:18.337
Sorge,

00:03:20.019 --> 00:03:20.838
I'm under arrest.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:35.520
The man whose mission it was to avoid war is charged with violating the law to protect the peace.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.081
In a cynical double-cross of betrayal,

00:03:39.641 --> 00:03:42.084
Zorga is the one who is ultimately betrayed.

00:03:42.843 --> 00:03:43.985
At the crucial moment,

00:03:44.225 --> 00:03:48.887
the later hero of the Soviet Union is disowned by both friend and foe alike.

00:03:51.916 --> 00:03:53.358
The ultimate anti-hero.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:58.383
He allows his life's work to be documented while in Japanese custody.

00:03:59.743 --> 00:04:05.370
It is both bitter and tragic that world history is not the only thing that could have been very different.

00:04:07.972 --> 00:04:13.017
If I had lived under peaceful social conditions and been surrounded by peaceful political developments,

00:04:13.418 --> 00:04:14.819
I might have become a scientist.

00:04:16.342 --> 00:04:16.963
In any case,

00:04:17.263 --> 00:04:18.284
certainly not a spy.

00:04:20.906 --> 00:04:21.707
Richard Sorga,

00:04:21.787 --> 00:04:23.428
the spy that didn't want to be one,

00:04:23.468 --> 00:04:25.790
was born in Baku in 1895.

00:04:30.274 --> 00:04:31.395
His mother was Russian,

00:04:31.535 --> 00:04:32.496
his father German.

00:04:33.076 --> 00:04:35.558
Two peoples that would define Sorga's life.

00:04:38.241 --> 00:04:42.304
Wilhelm Sorga works as an engineer for oil drilling machines in Azerbaijan,

00:04:42.484 --> 00:04:44.426
part of the Tsar's empire at the time.

00:04:45.966 --> 00:04:48.588
The family occupies a villa on the Caspian Sea.

00:04:50.811 --> 00:04:53.513
Richard Sorge is no child of the proletariat.

00:04:54.034 --> 00:04:54.955
At the age of three,

00:04:54.995 --> 00:04:56.376
his family moves to Berlin.

00:04:57.517 --> 00:04:58.078
In prison,

00:04:58.138 --> 00:05:00.040
he described his childhood like this.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.581
Until the war broke out,

00:05:01.882 --> 00:05:06.086
I enjoyed the relative security commonly found among the prosperous German bourgeoisie.

00:05:11.593 --> 00:05:12.855
With the outbreak of the war,

00:05:13.055 --> 00:05:13.175
the

00:05:13.574 --> 00:05:18.516
18-year-old Sorga immediately registers himself as a volunteer to fight for his fatherland.

00:05:19.456 --> 00:05:24.399
The young man's exuberance dissipates when faced with the carnage on the battlefields of Flanders.

00:05:27.961 --> 00:05:29.822
He is wounded multiple times.

00:05:30.102 --> 00:05:30.622
In the end,

00:05:30.682 --> 00:05:32.703
his left leg is shredded by shrapnel,

00:05:32.862 --> 00:05:34.804
and he barely avoids an amputation.

00:05:36.184 --> 00:05:38.165
Sorga is left with a lifelong limp,

00:05:38.444 --> 00:05:40.086
an Iron Cross second class,

00:05:40.586 --> 00:05:44.048
and the conviction that such a slaughter must never be repeated.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.032
This wild bloody brawl shook me to my core.

00:05:51.273 --> 00:05:53.795
How pointless are these endlessly repeating wars?

00:05:58.018 --> 00:06:00.620
Convinced of the peacemaking power of communism,

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:04.162
the young man devotes himself to the ideas of Marx and Engels.

00:06:06.224 --> 00:06:09.166
Sorge takes part in the Kiel Mutiny in 1918.

00:06:09.366 --> 00:06:13.568
and is active as an anti-capitalist agitator amongst the miners in Aachen.

00:06:13.569 --> 00:06:21.013
In 1919,

00:06:21.073 --> 00:06:25.675
he receives his PhD in political science and joins the German Communist Party.

00:06:32.359 --> 00:06:36.302
The new decade turns Berlin into the most sinful metropolis in Europe.

00:06:37.794 --> 00:06:39.715
The prudish imperial age is over.

00:06:40.616 --> 00:06:41.156
The roaring

00:06:41.576 --> 00:06:43.217
20s usher in passion and vice,

00:06:43.956 --> 00:06:46.059
and a new era in art and fashion.

00:06:47.579 --> 00:06:53.423
No one has yet noticed that the humiliation of the lost war is gnawing at the foundations of the decade.

00:06:54.763 --> 00:06:57.465
The spirit of optimism hasn't captured everyone.

00:06:57.925 --> 00:07:00.086
Inflation is eating away at everything,

00:07:00.406 --> 00:07:02.107
including trust in democracy.

00:07:03.487 --> 00:07:06.569
The lines of social division are becoming ever more apparent.

00:07:09.997 --> 00:07:14.762
The World War from 1914 to 1918 influenced my life from the ground up.

00:07:16.203 --> 00:07:18.425
Even if other considerations had not played a role,

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:20.906
that war alone would have made me a communist.

00:07:28.033 --> 00:07:29.033
While in Frankfurt,

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:32.857
Sorga comes into contact with senior officials of the Communist International.

00:07:32.997 --> 00:07:36.000
They invite him to collaborate with them in their Moscow headquarters.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.011
Sorge does his job well.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:47.894
He is accepted into the CPSU and dispatched to other European countries.

00:07:52.475 --> 00:07:55.877
He draws the attention of the Soviet Military Intelligence Services.

00:07:56.177 --> 00:07:57.379
General Jan Bersin,

00:07:57.478 --> 00:07:58.819
leader of the 4th Division,

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.641
recruits Sorge for his network of agents in China.

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:06.644
Before Sorge begins his journey,

00:08:07.004 --> 00:08:09.906
he meets the young acting student Katya Maksimova.

00:08:12.162 --> 00:08:13.882
It is one of many romances,

00:08:14.083 --> 00:08:14.682
but for him,

00:08:14.823 --> 00:08:16.203
the most significant one.

00:08:24.985 --> 00:08:25.526
In Berlin,

00:08:25.865 --> 00:08:32.628
Sorga acquires two publishers who offer to use their status as legal employers to disguise him as a German journalist.

00:08:33.827 --> 00:08:34.347
In China,

00:08:34.748 --> 00:08:37.089
Sorga's new area of operation has an agent.

00:08:37.408 --> 00:08:40.629
Two civil war parties are fighting over control of the country.

00:08:41.217 --> 00:08:48.620
The Russians and the Americans provide their minions with assistance in an attempt to secure their respective influence in the Middle Kingdom.

00:08:53.081 --> 00:08:53.780
On January 10,

00:08:53.782 --> 00:08:54.961
1930,

00:08:55.341 --> 00:08:58.543
the German journalist Richard Sorge arrives in Shanghai.

00:08:59.322 --> 00:09:01.764
The city is known as the Paris of the East,

00:09:02.303 --> 00:09:03.543
the New York of the West,

00:09:04.423 --> 00:09:06.865
a metropolis with cosmopolitan character,

00:09:07.205 --> 00:09:08.466
a synonym for sin,

00:09:08.725 --> 00:09:09.346
adventure,

00:09:09.446 --> 00:09:09.966
and wealth.

00:09:11.137 --> 00:09:12.038
In 1930,

00:09:12.237 --> 00:09:14.838
Shanghai boasts the highest skyscrapers in Asia.

00:09:15.158 --> 00:09:17.699
They belong to merchants and industrial companies.

00:09:18.939 --> 00:09:22.740
It is no coincidence that China's Communist Party is taking root here,

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.761
and announcing its fight against foreign imperialists.

00:09:34.584 --> 00:09:36.064
Under the code name Ramsey,

00:09:36.504 --> 00:09:39.346
Zorga begins to build a network of communist agents.

00:09:40.341 --> 00:09:42.203
In this city of over a million people,

00:09:42.423 --> 00:09:43.084
this jungle,

00:09:43.304 --> 00:09:45.525
flickering with chaotic rumors and secrets,

00:09:45.725 --> 00:09:55.591
anyone looking for a conspiratorial place in which people betray top-secret information and are in constant fear of being betrayed themselves would do well to turn up at the Peace Hotel.

00:09:56.153 --> 00:10:01.235
It was here that Richard Sorge met the American journalist and comm intern agent Agnes Smedley,

00:10:01.876 --> 00:10:03.357
a well-known expert on China.

00:10:11.289 --> 00:10:16.421
He builds up his contacts on the one hand through Russian communists who are already residing in China.

00:10:17.163 --> 00:10:17.865
On the other hand...

00:10:18.393 --> 00:10:20.095
through communists like Agnes Smedley,

00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:23.118
who is closely linked to the Chinese communists at that time,

00:10:23.658 --> 00:10:26.621
and who turns to SORGA and thus changes employers,

00:10:26.681 --> 00:10:27.262
so to speak.

00:10:27.922 --> 00:10:30.165
She no longer works solely for the Chinese.

00:10:30.385 --> 00:10:32.507
She now also works for the Soviet Union.

00:10:34.729 --> 00:10:41.055
Agnes Smedley introduces SORGA to the Japanese newspaper correspondent and expert on Japanese China policy,

00:10:41.396 --> 00:10:42.497
Okazi Hosumi.

00:10:43.669 --> 00:10:48.310
He is a convinced communist and an opponent of Japanese delusions of grandeur in Asia.

00:10:52.712 --> 00:10:54.132
On September 31,

00:10:54.133 --> 00:10:57.533
Japan attacks and annexes the enormous Chinese province,

00:10:57.773 --> 00:10:58.373
Manchuria.

00:11:01.554 --> 00:11:03.515
The proclamation of the satellite state,

00:11:03.575 --> 00:11:04.055
Manchukuo,

00:11:04.335 --> 00:11:11.177
and a bloodbath among the civilian population in Shanghai are only the earliest signs of the Japanese becoming drunk with power.

00:11:11.545 --> 00:11:14.647
and wanting to first subjugate their historical enemy China,

00:11:14.867 --> 00:11:16.649
and then the whole of the Far East.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.132
I felt compelled to dive into the problem of Japan as a whole,

00:11:21.592 --> 00:11:24.954
and I decided to prepare myself generally as long as I was in China,

00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:31.039
to thoroughly familiarize myself with Japanese history and Japan's diplomatic traditions and practices.

00:11:38.624 --> 00:11:39.685
Sorge and Osaki

00:11:40.153 --> 00:11:41.935
regularly met on Nanjing Road,

00:11:42.595 --> 00:11:45.238
one of the largest shopping streets in the world at the time.

00:11:46.559 --> 00:11:50.342
Ozaki would unpack his knowledge about Japanese intentions in China.

00:11:51.183 --> 00:11:53.305
Sorgan forms headquarters in Moscow.

00:11:54.026 --> 00:11:55.007
They are impressed.

00:11:56.928 --> 00:12:01.112
The effects of the global economic crisis are less stark in Asia than in the West.

00:12:02.113 --> 00:12:03.034
The hardships of the

00:12:03.855 --> 00:12:06.037
1930s paved the way for socialism.

00:12:07.357 --> 00:12:11.400
The NSDAP takes power in the German Reich in 1933,

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:12.921
and the new Reich Chancellor,

00:12:13.081 --> 00:12:13.781
Adolf Hitler,

00:12:13.982 --> 00:12:15.663
outlines the goals of his policies.

00:12:16.163 --> 00:12:18.164
To conquer new living space in the East,

00:12:18.645 --> 00:12:20.366
and to ruthlessly Germanize it.

00:12:22.307 --> 00:12:26.750
The next great catastrophe looms.

00:12:27.211 --> 00:12:30.313
Stalin was very interested in having spies in Japan,

00:12:31.013 --> 00:12:36.197
because the Japanese military made it very clear that the Soviet Union was enemy number one.

00:12:40.524 --> 00:12:42.085
People are alarmed in Moscow.

00:12:42.906 --> 00:12:45.028
After so easily conquering Manchuria,

00:12:45.188 --> 00:12:47.850
the Japanese military might start craving more.

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:49.912
And at this critical point in time,

00:12:50.092 --> 00:12:53.895
Russian military intelligence doesn't have any spy network in Japan.

00:12:57.998 --> 00:12:58.519
In Japan,

00:12:59.079 --> 00:13:01.601
there was an extremely strong defense against spies.

00:13:02.662 --> 00:13:05.585
They never let the workers of the Soviet embassy out of their sight.

00:13:07.418 --> 00:13:10.522
The whole Russian colony was under constant surveillance.

00:13:11.382 --> 00:13:14.045
We needed information and we needed it immediately.

00:13:15.407 --> 00:13:21.012
The only way out was to fall back on foreign agents that one didn't have to train.

00:13:22.734 --> 00:13:29.060
But Stalin did not trust foreigners.

00:13:31.257 --> 00:13:31.937
Nevertheless,

00:13:32.078 --> 00:13:35.760
the foreigner's Zorga received orders to build a spy ring in Tokyo.

00:13:37.621 --> 00:13:43.524
He is charged with scouting out both Japan's military strength and if they plan to attack the Soviet Union.

00:13:50.007 --> 00:13:50.648
At this time,

00:13:50.848 --> 00:13:52.809
Japan is the main source of information.

00:13:53.589 --> 00:13:55.010
You have to know what Japan wants,

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.932
because Japan is the defining power in East Asia.

00:13:59.212 --> 00:14:00.373
Before his departure,

00:14:00.673 --> 00:14:04.075
Sorge convinces his lover Katya Maksimova to marry him.

00:14:04.996 --> 00:14:08.117
She would be better off as the wife of an officer of the Red Army.

00:14:09.358 --> 00:14:11.919
It is a decision that Katya will later regret.

00:14:14.401 --> 00:14:17.202
In order to avoid the strictly controlled route to the Far East,

00:14:17.502 --> 00:14:19.604
Richard Sorge travels through the U.S.

00:14:19.664 --> 00:14:20.644
on his way to Asia.

00:14:20.944 --> 00:14:24.266
He meets up with members of the American Comintern in New York.

00:14:25.007 --> 00:14:25.827
Eight years later,

00:14:25.887 --> 00:14:28.949
the connection to Japanese communists in the USA will...

00:14:29.293 --> 00:14:30.354
Almost by accident,

00:14:30.754 --> 00:14:34.636
tip off the Japanese secret police to the existence of the spy ring.

00:14:37.898 --> 00:14:38.578
On September 6th,

00:14:38.579 --> 00:14:40.820
1933,

00:14:40.821 --> 00:14:42.320
Sorge arrives in Yokohama.

00:14:43.021 --> 00:14:46.383
Japan has a long tradition of imitating Western countries.

00:14:46.903 --> 00:14:47.123
Law,

00:14:47.563 --> 00:14:47.803
army,

00:14:48.124 --> 00:14:49.104
industrial goods,

00:14:49.424 --> 00:14:50.085
all copied,

00:14:50.365 --> 00:14:51.586
especially from Germany.

00:14:51.886 --> 00:14:55.608
And yet the transition into modern times has not yet fully materialized,

00:14:55.708 --> 00:14:57.609
and Japanese society is divided.

00:14:57.869 --> 00:14:59.631
even in the highest centers of power.

00:15:01.814 --> 00:15:02.374
The emperor,

00:15:02.555 --> 00:15:04.597
who himself rejects militarism,

00:15:04.837 --> 00:15:08.562
is threatening to become a compliant tool in the hands of a confident military,

00:15:08.842 --> 00:15:11.685
one that is vehemently propagating war against Russia.

00:15:14.929 --> 00:15:18.373
Stalin needs spies who can deliver reliable reports about the

00:15:18.373 --> 00:15:20.214
The course being charted by Japan.

00:15:21.774 --> 00:15:23.414
The routes used by his messengers,

00:15:23.614 --> 00:15:26.875
bringing secret files over Shanghai or Hong Kong to Moscow,

00:15:27.075 --> 00:15:29.556
is threatened by the Second Sino-Japanese War.

00:15:29.836 --> 00:15:32.737
Radio transmissions are thus becoming ever more important.

00:15:38.799 --> 00:15:41.900
Things became difficult in 1940-41,

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:46.641
when the colleagues in the Soviet embassy in Japan came into direct contact with Saga.

00:15:47.081 --> 00:15:51.044
It was an inconceivable violation of the basic principles of conspiracy,

00:15:51.485 --> 00:15:53.466
because of course they were under observation.

00:15:57.929 --> 00:15:59.551
Sorge operates brazenly.

00:15:59.831 --> 00:16:00.792
He builds a roughly

00:16:01.272 --> 00:16:10.119
40-person spy ring directly under the noses of the Japanese secret police and infiltrates not only the inner circles of Japanese politicians and soldiers,

00:16:10.279 --> 00:16:11.940
but also of the German elite.

00:16:14.117 --> 00:16:18.561
I thought that I would appear more reliable in the eyes of the Japanese if I won the trust of the embassy,

00:16:18.941 --> 00:16:22.584
and that the embassy would serve as a bulwark against any doubts about my person.

00:16:25.927 --> 00:16:30.130
Richard Sorge begins to conquer the German embassy and its surroundings.

00:16:31.591 --> 00:16:31.872
Soon,

00:16:31.992 --> 00:16:34.073
he is a known figure in the German colony,

00:16:34.334 --> 00:16:38.177
one that readily enjoys the back-home flair of the German establishment.

00:16:44.025 --> 00:16:44.686
Even today,

00:16:44.966 --> 00:16:49.008
the Imperial Hotel is an ideal place for more discreet meetings.

00:16:52.111 --> 00:16:56.153
It is the bar of the Imperial Hotel in the immediate vicinity of the Imperial Palace,

00:16:56.353 --> 00:16:59.796
and it was the central meeting place for both the German community and others.

00:17:00.416 --> 00:17:00.896
In the end,

00:17:00.957 --> 00:17:06.380
the information that Sorge became so famous for procuring certainly came from German sources,

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.261
but especially from government sources.

00:17:10.623 --> 00:17:13.325
It is actually an international meeting place.

00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:16.999
The various media representatives from around the globe meet there.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:18.320
Diplomats,

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:19.581
business leaders,

00:17:19.801 --> 00:17:20.962
business representatives.

00:17:22.123 --> 00:17:25.125
It was the kind of place where you could gather relevant information,

00:17:25.425 --> 00:17:26.886
engage in harmless conversation,

00:17:27.486 --> 00:17:28.367
background talks.

00:17:31.649 --> 00:17:37.033
Comrade Branko Vukolic is responsible for transferring secret materials onto microfilm.

00:17:39.321 --> 00:17:45.086
As it came to light after Sorga's unmasking that his network extended to the very highest levels of the government,

00:17:45.626 --> 00:17:52.972
people began asking how a European was able to dive so deeply into this seemingly impermeable Japanese society.

00:17:55.434 --> 00:17:58.597
Sorga has made himself into an expert on his host country,

00:17:58.977 --> 00:18:01.119
and he counts on Japanese accomplices.

00:18:05.162 --> 00:18:08.485
The artist Miyagi Yotoku is recruited in the U.S.

00:18:08.901 --> 00:18:10.162
And Ozaki Hotsumi,

00:18:10.542 --> 00:18:12.342
whom Sorga knows from Shanghai,

00:18:12.483 --> 00:18:14.523
is immediately ready to cooperate.

00:18:16.744 --> 00:18:17.865
In the following years,

00:18:18.485 --> 00:18:21.006
Sorga and Ozaki meet at different locations,

00:18:21.586 --> 00:18:23.087
seldom at Ozaki's home,

00:18:23.867 --> 00:18:24.627
out of caution,

00:18:26.468 --> 00:18:28.469
often in changing places in Tokyo,

00:18:29.169 --> 00:18:31.170
on street corners or in restaurants.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:34.972
The two exchange news and discuss assignments together.

00:18:39.453 --> 00:18:42.435
Saga's intellectual efforts were adding to his prestige.

00:18:43.875 --> 00:18:47.537
Ambassador Ott valued Saga's analysis of Japan very highly.

00:18:47.777 --> 00:18:51.999
He had even commissioned Saga to write reports that he was supposed to have authored himself.

00:18:52.759 --> 00:18:53.379
Intellectually,

00:18:53.899 --> 00:18:55.660
Saga was moving on a very high level.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:56.761
Ozaki as well.

00:18:57.221 --> 00:18:58.641
He came from a top university,

00:18:58.922 --> 00:18:59.882
belonged to the elite,

00:19:00.142 --> 00:19:01.223
spoke good Chinese,

00:19:01.343 --> 00:19:05.684
was an expert in Chinese politics and could precisely assess developments.

00:19:07.877 --> 00:19:14.363
What set their sparring apart from others was that they themselves could submit political suggestions to Stalin.

00:19:23.291 --> 00:19:30.097
Sorge's political essays establish his reputation in Germany as an expert on Asia and a serious journalist.

00:19:30.437 --> 00:19:34.401
His inclusion in the NSDAP completes his perfect disguise.

00:19:40.725 --> 00:19:42.946
He had laid the foundation for his work.

00:19:43.446 --> 00:19:47.847
The German officers and officials in Tokyo trust Sorge and his expertise.

00:19:48.288 --> 00:19:49.288
First and foremost,

00:19:49.328 --> 00:19:51.909
the military attaché and later ambassador,

00:19:52.189 --> 00:19:52.849
Eugen Ott.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:56.130
Without this knowledge,

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:57.671
I mean my thorough research,

00:19:58.431 --> 00:20:04.493
no one working at the embassy would have been interested in speaking with me about things or asking my advice on confidential matters.

00:20:12.613 --> 00:20:17.955
Richard Sorger is always welcome at social events and gains a reputation as an eccentric,

00:20:18.055 --> 00:20:19.176
hard-drinking ladies'

00:20:19.216 --> 00:20:19.436
man.

00:20:20.997 --> 00:20:24.858
Erwin Wickert was a broadcasting attaché in Tokyo at the time.

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:30.140
Sorger was a very attractive man.

00:20:31.321 --> 00:20:34.822
Once he was dancing very intensively with my mother at a ball.

00:20:35.623 --> 00:20:38.564
So much so that my father went over and said,

00:20:38.884 --> 00:20:39.444
Come on now,

00:20:39.824 --> 00:20:40.325
that's enough.

00:20:43.305 --> 00:20:48.708
He always had the feeling that Sorge was a person who had a very difficult time controlling himself.

00:20:52.671 --> 00:20:53.211
But sober,

00:20:53.571 --> 00:20:55.012
he must have been a pleasant guest,

00:20:55.272 --> 00:20:57.794
who obviously had quite an effect on women.

00:21:02.197 --> 00:21:05.959
An eternal stranger who condemns himself to never finding true peace.

00:21:11.005 --> 00:21:14.566
Sorge's own words and an expression of his deep loneliness.

00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:18.028
Under the weight of secrets that he can share with no one,

00:21:18.548 --> 00:21:19.829
Sorge begins drinking,

00:21:20.209 --> 00:21:21.549
often without restraint.

00:21:27.972 --> 00:21:28.692
When he was drunk,

00:21:29.132 --> 00:21:32.694
Richard Sorge would curse incredibly about the Nazis and Hitler.

00:21:33.434 --> 00:21:38.396
And my father would rent a room for Richard Sorge in the hotel in which my father also lived,

00:21:39.276 --> 00:21:40.357
so that he could sleep there.

00:21:40.757 --> 00:21:42.719
and didn't have to ride home on his motorcycle.

00:21:45.161 --> 00:21:49.385
Again and again,

00:21:49.825 --> 00:21:52.528
Sorge rides his motorcycle in a drunken stupor,

00:21:52.948 --> 00:21:55.691
until he ends up against a wall with a broken skull.

00:21:56.231 --> 00:21:57.853
When he is released from the hospital,

00:21:57.993 --> 00:21:59.795
the Otts take extra care of him.

00:22:01.756 --> 00:22:06.361
The love affair between Sorge and Otts wife Helma seems almost inevitable.

00:22:12.983 --> 00:22:15.165
Zogha was a university assistant in Aachen.

00:22:15.845 --> 00:22:20.129
His professor there was married to a very young woman who Zogha stole away from him.

00:22:20.929 --> 00:22:22.030
She divorced her husband,

00:22:22.390 --> 00:22:23.051
married Zogha,

00:22:23.591 --> 00:22:24.852
and went with him to Moscow.

00:22:26.614 --> 00:22:29.076
But even after Zogha married the wife of his professor,

00:22:29.396 --> 00:22:30.997
the two worked together amicably.

00:22:32.018 --> 00:22:32.438
Strange,

00:22:32.458 --> 00:22:32.699
right?

00:22:33.419 --> 00:22:35.541
He even slept with Ambassador Ott's wife.

00:22:36.161 --> 00:22:37.202
It wasn't a nice story,

00:22:37.502 --> 00:22:40.864
but it is astounding that Ott also continued working with Sorge.

00:22:48.048 --> 00:22:51.310
The marriage to Katia did not prevent other adventures.

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:56.053
If the affair with the ambassador's wife really took place remains disputed.

00:22:56.873 --> 00:23:00.936
It could have cost Sorge his own neck and his best information source,

00:23:01.176 --> 00:23:02.437
Eugen Ott as well.

00:23:06.314 --> 00:23:09.497
The relationship between Sorge and Ott is difficult to describe.

00:23:10.578 --> 00:23:13.661
From the literature we can gather that they were very close acquaintances,

00:23:13.781 --> 00:23:14.982
if not outright friends,

00:23:15.582 --> 00:23:17.304
but nonetheless not without mistrust.

00:23:17.564 --> 00:23:22.509
But the mistrust was not so much related to the personal relationship between Sorge and the ambassador's wife,

00:23:22.969 --> 00:23:28.194
but rather regarding the question of if Sorge isn't a bit too thoughtless when he has had too much to drink,

00:23:28.594 --> 00:23:31.657
shares too much of the personal information that he has with Ott.

00:23:34.741 --> 00:23:36.442
In May 1935,

00:23:36.783 --> 00:23:38.444
Sorgas called back to Moscow.

00:23:38.644 --> 00:23:40.946
A number of his fellow spies have disappeared,

00:23:41.146 --> 00:23:42.206
including his mentor,

00:23:42.387 --> 00:23:43.187
General Bezin.

00:23:44.128 --> 00:23:44.948
His successors,

00:23:45.049 --> 00:23:47.070
Generals Zuritsky and Artusov,

00:23:47.430 --> 00:23:49.412
also failed to survive their appointments.

00:23:53.595 --> 00:23:58.118
Operations against spies with a foreign background began in 1936.

00:23:59.079 --> 00:23:59.559
Poles,

00:23:59.879 --> 00:24:00.460
Latvians,

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:01.380
Lithuanians,

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:01.941
Finns...

00:24:02.517 --> 00:24:07.079
Representatives of practically all of the Soviet member states were either harassed,

00:24:07.559 --> 00:24:08.159
ordered back,

00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:09.900
stuck in camps or shot.

00:24:12.441 --> 00:24:15.543
You could say that Stalin destroyed his secret service.

00:24:15.763 --> 00:24:16.223
In fact,

00:24:16.783 --> 00:24:18.004
he annihilated it.

00:24:20.365 --> 00:24:23.746
No one in Moscow feels safe in the face of Stalin's whims,

00:24:24.006 --> 00:24:27.108
especially not Richard Zorga with his German passport.

00:24:27.228 --> 00:24:28.948
He will never see Moscow again,

00:24:29.188 --> 00:24:30.289
nor his wife Katya.

00:24:31.801 --> 00:24:34.542
But Sorga remains true to Stalin to the end.

00:24:35.002 --> 00:24:36.403
Is he turning a blind eye?

00:24:41.886 --> 00:24:50.389
Sorga was more of an ideological communist than a party member and held the view that Stalin was still a lesser evil compared to the Nazis.

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:52.991
Given world events,

00:24:53.371 --> 00:24:53.991
he definitely...

00:24:54.091 --> 00:24:57.213
thought that the fall of Nazi Germany was the most important thing,

00:24:57.393 --> 00:25:01.035
and that as long as the Soviet Union was standing together with the US,

00:25:01.216 --> 00:25:03.237
France and England against the Nazis,

00:25:03.557 --> 00:25:09.881
he could contribute to bringing about the quickest end to the war by continuing to provide information to the Soviet Union.

00:25:13.323 --> 00:25:14.384
Sorge's signalman,

00:25:14.624 --> 00:25:15.444
Max Clausen,

00:25:15.845 --> 00:25:20.588
first achieved exactly that at the beginning of 1936 through radio transmission.

00:25:21.108 --> 00:25:22.409
But the work is dangerous.

00:25:22.821 --> 00:25:25.922
The Japanese listening posts can receive the illicit signals,

00:25:26.122 --> 00:25:28.183
even if they can't locate them precisely.

00:25:28.683 --> 00:25:28.963
Soon,

00:25:29.063 --> 00:25:31.804
they are certain that a spy is operating out of Tokyo.

00:25:32.484 --> 00:25:33.544
Risking their lives,

00:25:33.724 --> 00:25:36.685
agents from around the world are sending secrets to Moscow.

00:25:36.885 --> 00:25:39.746
Only some of these actually reach the apex of the Kremlin,

00:25:40.106 --> 00:25:43.127
because whatever seemed unimportant would simply be thrown out.

00:25:46.288 --> 00:25:46.968
On top of that,

00:25:47.468 --> 00:25:49.188
Stalin didn't want any analysis,

00:25:49.529 --> 00:25:51.149
just pure raw information.

00:25:52.283 --> 00:25:52.723
He said,

00:25:53.284 --> 00:25:58.046
give me the information and I'll draw my own conclusions.

00:26:02.649 --> 00:26:03.550
Sorge's article,

00:26:03.650 --> 00:26:04.670
Revolt in Tokyo,

00:26:04.790 --> 00:26:07.612
about the failed military coup in 1936,

00:26:07.712 --> 00:26:09.893
is one of the most read internationally.

00:26:12.335 --> 00:26:17.058
His brilliant analysis of the events finally opened all of the doors of the embassy to him.

00:26:17.398 --> 00:26:19.059
He even gets his own office there.

00:26:21.211 --> 00:26:22.412
Shortly after the coup,

00:26:22.692 --> 00:26:25.533
the military attaché Ott asks Dr.

00:26:25.633 --> 00:26:26.534
Sorge for help.

00:26:28.255 --> 00:26:30.336
I had to swear to him that I would tell no one.

00:26:31.417 --> 00:26:34.939
I did that and helped him to encrypt the telegram in his apartment.

00:26:36.019 --> 00:26:41.162
Ott had asked me for help and not a member of the embassy because the matter required the utmost secrecy.

00:26:45.945 --> 00:26:49.947
My father actually described Ott as a rather reserved ambassador.

00:26:51.876 --> 00:26:54.297
And even when he knew Sorge very well,

00:26:55.918 --> 00:26:59.760
my father always assumed that he was obviously not very affable.

00:26:59.921 --> 00:27:02.002
And also,

00:27:02.242 --> 00:27:06.825
he didn't know where Sorge was getting his information.

00:27:12.368 --> 00:27:16.671
Sorge not only finds out the secret code of the communication traffic with Berlin,

00:27:16.871 --> 00:27:20.893
but also the details of top-secret German-Japanese negotiations.

00:27:21.493 --> 00:27:26.155
When the anti-com intern pact between Germany and Japan is signed in November of 36,

00:27:26.555 --> 00:27:28.356
Stalin is very well informed.

00:27:29.316 --> 00:27:31.637
The pact is aimed against the Soviet Union.

00:27:38.380 --> 00:27:43.703
From the nearly 700 reports that Sorge had sent,

00:27:44.835 --> 00:27:47.356
More than half were actually presented to the leadership,

00:27:48.236 --> 00:27:52.237
including Stalin.

00:27:52.697 --> 00:27:57.499
These reports were assessed as especially valuable.

00:27:57.979 --> 00:28:00.820
That speaks to the fact that Zaga was an exceptional spy.

00:28:03.801 --> 00:28:09.602
I believe it is a unique case in the history of the Secret Services.

00:28:16.127 --> 00:28:19.148
The Japanese continue with their raid in northern China.

00:28:20.569 --> 00:28:21.989
But the Chinese fight back,

00:28:22.230 --> 00:28:26.091
and the Japanese continually ask for more help from the China expert,

00:28:26.411 --> 00:28:27.431
Ozaki Hotsumi.

00:28:28.212 --> 00:28:29.752
The Japanese Prime Minister,

00:28:29.952 --> 00:28:30.352
Konoe,

00:28:30.712 --> 00:28:33.213
takes on Ozaki as a governmental advisor.

00:28:34.234 --> 00:28:38.015
Zorga's spy ring has penetrated the center of Japanese power.

00:28:44.247 --> 00:28:46.309
It is a critical moment for the Russians,

00:28:46.550 --> 00:28:47.371
as their own man,

00:28:47.491 --> 00:28:48.472
General Yushkov,

00:28:48.592 --> 00:28:51.335
defects to the Japanese out of fear of Stalin.

00:28:53.818 --> 00:28:57.362
They are about to extend the border of the state of Manchukuo to the north.

00:28:57.662 --> 00:28:58.423
Near Nomohan,

00:28:58.483 --> 00:29:00.205
they face off against the Red Army,

00:29:00.525 --> 00:29:03.749
about which they now hold valuable information in their hands.

00:29:11.435 --> 00:29:17.298
Sorga receives the urgent order from Moscow to make copies of the documents that the deserter has handed over.

00:29:17.799 --> 00:29:19.880
What does the enemy know about the Red Army?

00:29:22.261 --> 00:29:24.262
Sorga's report proves invaluable.

00:29:24.823 --> 00:29:30.326
The Russians change their troop formations and gain the upper hand against a confused Japanese force.

00:29:32.727 --> 00:29:35.008
Shocked by the loss of more than 8,000 men,

00:29:35.289 --> 00:29:39.431
the Empire must reconsider its goal of expanding into the Soviet Union.

00:29:43.515 --> 00:29:44.776
From secret documents,

00:29:44.916 --> 00:29:48.799
it emerges that Berlin is trying to make use of the rethinking process.

00:29:50.461 --> 00:29:56.065
The German diplomats in Tokyo are instructed to prepare the way for a military alliance with Japan.

00:30:01.029 --> 00:30:08.135
Hitler is planning a war against England and France and wants to obligate Japan to attack the British colonies in the Far East.

00:30:10.117 --> 00:30:12.819
But Japan is caught up in its war against China.

00:30:13.039 --> 00:30:14.661
and doesn't want to become involved.

00:30:14.921 --> 00:30:19.225
Germany responds with anger and signs a non-aggression pact with the Soviet Union.

00:30:19.565 --> 00:30:20.586
For the Japanese,

00:30:20.786 --> 00:30:22.047
this smells like betrayal.

00:30:25.550 --> 00:30:31.556
Japan had always hoped that Germany would take Japan's side in a war against the Soviet Union as a matter of principle.

00:30:31.896 --> 00:30:33.257
But with the non-aggression pact,

00:30:33.518 --> 00:30:34.438
that was not possible.

00:30:35.059 --> 00:30:35.539
In the end,

00:30:35.860 --> 00:30:39.503
the Anti-Komitean Pact of 1936 had lost its meaning.

00:30:40.059 --> 00:30:42.807
because the potential enemy was no longer the Soviet Union,

00:30:42.967 --> 00:30:45.694
at least if international agreements were to be taken seriously.

00:30:47.217 --> 00:30:47.477
Thus,

00:30:47.597 --> 00:30:53.822
it also represented an opportunity for Japan to sign a neutrality pact with the Soviet Union in 1941,

00:30:54.222 --> 00:30:56.964
and the war took a different course than had originally been planned,

00:30:57.064 --> 00:30:58.525
at least by the strategists.

00:31:01.187 --> 00:31:03.549
In order to stop Japan's advance in Asia,

00:31:03.869 --> 00:31:06.611
the US cancelled its trade agreement with Japan,

00:31:06.931 --> 00:31:11.034
thereby substantially shutting off the oil tap for the Japanese in the West.

00:31:12.175 --> 00:31:13.196
breaks out in Europe.

00:31:13.316 --> 00:31:18.618
as the German armed forces march into Poland and begin an unprecedented war of conquest.

00:31:20.859 --> 00:31:25.721
It only stands to reason that Japan will now form an alliance with the victorious Germans.

00:31:31.484 --> 00:31:36.546
Ribbentrop sends Special Envoy Stammer to Tokyo for talks with Foreign Minister Matsuoka.

00:31:37.466 --> 00:31:38.807
During the negotiations,

00:31:39.107 --> 00:31:41.468
Sorge maintains close relations with Stammer.

00:31:41.884 --> 00:31:43.945
He has recently become the press attaché,

00:31:44.325 --> 00:31:45.826
appointed by Ambassador Ott,

00:31:46.126 --> 00:31:47.946
seen here in a celebratory mood.

00:31:53.689 --> 00:31:56.310
Long before the signing of the Tripartite Pact,

00:31:56.530 --> 00:31:59.891
Stalin learns that Japan has joined the Rome-Berlin axis.

00:32:04.793 --> 00:32:10.536
The alliance intends to direct itself against England and to deter the Americans from entering the war.

00:32:15.453 --> 00:32:18.215
The nerve-wracking work of spying takes its toll.

00:32:19.056 --> 00:32:23.139
Signalman Clausen suffers a heart attack and is no longer fully in the game.

00:32:23.860 --> 00:32:25.961
Important reports are left unsent.

00:32:26.842 --> 00:32:30.685
Sorge asks once again after 11 years to be called back.

00:32:34.668 --> 00:32:36.609
There are a lot of examples where these people,

00:32:36.829 --> 00:32:39.111
when they have worked for the other side for years,

00:32:40.192 --> 00:32:40.752
For example,

00:32:41.053 --> 00:32:46.677
I'm thinking about the members of the Cambridge Five who became severe alcoholics because they simply couldn't deal with the pressure.

00:32:48.378 --> 00:32:49.779
The uncertainty and the pressure,

00:32:50.560 --> 00:32:56.104
and always having to think about what you talk about with whom and having to hide things even from those closest to you.

00:32:56.804 --> 00:32:58.886
Many people can't deal with that pressure over time.

00:33:00.927 --> 00:33:07.552
Sorge's request comes at a bad time because the spy ring is entering a decisive phase at the end of 1940.

00:33:08.504 --> 00:33:09.024
On December

00:33:09.505 --> 00:33:14.109
18th, Hitler signs the Commissar Order in preparation for Operation Barbarossa,

00:33:14.329 --> 00:33:16.471
the German invasion of the Soviet Union.

00:33:18.772 --> 00:33:20.093
A mere 10 days later,

00:33:20.394 --> 00:33:22.535
Sorge can radio a warning to Moscow.

00:33:24.197 --> 00:33:25.998
Germans are gathering at the eastern border,

00:33:26.258 --> 00:33:27.159
including Romania,

00:33:27.540 --> 00:33:28.340
80 divisions.

00:33:30.442 --> 00:33:34.785
Germany is in a position to occupy areas of the USSR along the lines of Kharkov,

00:33:35.166 --> 00:33:36.467
Moscow and Leningrad.

00:33:37.408 --> 00:33:37.748
Ramsey.

00:33:41.124 --> 00:33:41.664
Meanwhile,

00:33:41.804 --> 00:33:44.706
Ribbentrop had changed his strategic priorities.

00:33:45.206 --> 00:33:48.267
He is no longer looking for Japan's support against England,

00:33:48.487 --> 00:33:53.049
but rather to have the Japanese take control of the Soviet Union in the Far East.

00:33:57.051 --> 00:33:59.532
A directive from Moscow arrives in Tokyo.

00:34:00.372 --> 00:34:04.754
Agents are to deliver a detailed report on the positions of the Japanese troops,

00:34:04.914 --> 00:34:09.056
from the number and position of the divisions down to the names of the commanders.

00:34:09.976 --> 00:34:12.597
No problem for Sorge's Japanese spies.

00:34:16.758 --> 00:34:17.398
On March 3,

00:34:17.399 --> 00:34:18.658
1941,

00:34:18.939 --> 00:34:21.399
Foreign Minister Matsuka travels to Berlin,

00:34:21.579 --> 00:34:21.859
Rome,

00:34:21.879 --> 00:34:22.520
and Moscow.

00:34:26.541 --> 00:34:30.802
He surprises the Germans by signing a neutrality agreement with the Soviets.

00:34:32.602 --> 00:34:35.683
Stalin evidently firmly believes in the pact with Hitler,

00:34:35.803 --> 00:34:38.364
and that Japan will ultimately attack to the south.

00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:43.543
At the beginning of May 1941,

00:34:43.544 --> 00:34:46.885
Sorge elicits more information from Moscow from a special envoy.

00:34:47.666 --> 00:34:51.910
German generals are making very low estimates of the Red Army's combat strength.

00:34:52.450 --> 00:34:55.753
They believe they can eliminate the Red Army within a matter of weeks.

00:34:59.316 --> 00:35:02.119
Stalin views Hitler's word as beyond question.

00:35:02.639 --> 00:35:06.282
His mistrust is directed far more at the spies in Tokyo.

00:35:08.868 --> 00:35:13.752
Precisely because Saga was sending that kind of precarious and important information to Moscow,

00:35:14.373 --> 00:35:17.976
Stalin began to suspect that Saga might be a double agent.

00:35:22.460 --> 00:35:23.921
From the way that Saga was,

00:35:24.642 --> 00:35:27.364
I can hardly imagine that he was a double agent.

00:35:28.545 --> 00:35:28.865
I mean,

00:35:29.546 --> 00:35:30.346
when he was drunk,

00:35:31.027 --> 00:35:34.430
he spoke belligerently about Hitler and the Nazis.

00:35:35.291 --> 00:35:36.572
He rejected them completely.

00:35:38.337 --> 00:35:38.797
Given that,

00:35:39.178 --> 00:35:40.079
I can't imagine it.

00:35:40.579 --> 00:35:40.699
But

00:35:41.340 --> 00:35:42.260
I don't know for certain.

00:35:44.222 --> 00:35:47.885
Doubts about Sorge's loyalty are also springing up in Berlin.

00:35:48.745 --> 00:35:53.009
Vague references to his past in the KPD raise alarming questions.

00:35:53.509 --> 00:35:54.490
Is Sorge a spy,

00:35:54.850 --> 00:35:55.671
a double agent,

00:35:55.971 --> 00:35:57.252
or even a triple agent?

00:35:59.234 --> 00:36:03.357
Colonel Meisinger is sent to Tokyo as a police attaché to investigate.

00:36:06.613 --> 00:36:08.053
Does Zorga sense the threat?

00:36:08.794 --> 00:36:11.734
The newcomer feels very much like a foreigner in Tokyo.

00:36:12.195 --> 00:36:14.295
Zorga offers himself as a drinking buddy.

00:36:14.815 --> 00:36:20.917
Meisinger is thankful and becomes dazzled by Zorga's excellent reputation at the embassy and his personal charm.

00:36:21.297 --> 00:36:23.158
The surveillance of Zorga is withdrawn.

00:36:25.818 --> 00:36:26.639
And in the embassy,

00:36:26.899 --> 00:36:29.179
no one doubts his absolute trustworthiness.

00:36:29.839 --> 00:36:31.320
He freely comes and goes,

00:36:31.700 --> 00:36:35.441
and has or manages to gain access to Hitler's biggest secrets.

00:36:40.804 --> 00:36:45.168
Berlin informs Ott that the German attack will begin in second half of June.

00:36:45.528 --> 00:36:47.490
Attack will take place along the front,

00:36:47.810 --> 00:36:49.932
main thrust against Moscow and Leningrad.

00:36:50.472 --> 00:36:57.317
Moscow receives Zorga's dramatic warning on June 20th.

00:36:59.859 --> 00:37:01.501
The war is about to begin.

00:37:05.089 --> 00:37:07.650
The information was only as good as it was useful.

00:37:08.190 --> 00:37:10.431
And the Soviet intelligence agencies were very,

00:37:10.511 --> 00:37:11.591
very weak in this sense,

00:37:12.351 --> 00:37:14.512
because they performed almost no analysis.

00:37:14.752 --> 00:37:15.152
Instead,

00:37:15.432 --> 00:37:18.153
the information was simply reported directly to the top.

00:37:19.633 --> 00:37:22.794
Stalin receives corroborating reports from other spies,

00:37:23.094 --> 00:37:28.396
but he does not believe that Hitler will open a war on two fronts and disregards all of the warnings.

00:37:32.597 --> 00:37:35.518
Stalin had written a comment on a telegram with a green pen,

00:37:35.958 --> 00:37:41.500
which was presented to Harnack and Schulze-Boysen on June 21,

00:37:41.560 --> 00:37:43.160
1941.

00:37:43.161 --> 00:37:43.940
To hell with that.

00:37:44.541 --> 00:37:45.821
It's English disinformation.

00:37:50.422 --> 00:37:54.223
He believed that it was targeted disinformation from British intelligence,

00:37:54.743 --> 00:37:58.044
aimed at propelling Germany and the Soviet Union into war.

00:38:01.906 --> 00:38:02.386
Yes,

00:38:02.607 --> 00:38:03.247
in this case,

00:38:03.588 --> 00:38:05.730
Stalin actually called Sorge an asshole.

00:38:09.874 --> 00:38:11.675
At the crack of dawn on June 22,

00:38:11.735 --> 00:38:13.217
1941,

00:38:13.537 --> 00:38:17.441
over three million German soldiers cross the border into the Soviet Union.

00:38:19.223 --> 00:38:21.165
Operation Barbarossa has begun.

00:38:21.825 --> 00:38:25.088
The soldiers of the Red Army are virtually thrown out of their beds.

00:38:32.587 --> 00:38:34.949
June 22 affected Zorga deeply.

00:38:35.869 --> 00:38:37.171
According to all the stories,

00:38:37.351 --> 00:38:40.554
prison records and the memories of agents Klausen and Miyagi,

00:38:42.775 --> 00:38:45.458
Zorga ran himself ragged on June 22.

00:38:46.018 --> 00:38:47.620
He binge drank the entire day.

00:38:52.084 --> 00:38:58.169
His bitterness over not being taken seriously in Moscow is accompanied by increasing delusions of grandeur.

00:39:00.093 --> 00:39:01.434
If anyone annihilates Hitler,

00:39:01.935 --> 00:39:02.375
then it's me,

00:39:02.876 --> 00:39:03.576
Richard Sorge.

00:39:04.698 --> 00:39:07.060
He evidently claimed in a drunken state,

00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:10.483
according to comments later gathered from a German girlfriend.

00:39:15.648 --> 00:39:16.049
And yet,

00:39:16.309 --> 00:39:20.073
what would have happened if Stalin had believed his spy?

00:39:22.025 --> 00:39:29.431
The Soviet Union now had to worry that Japan would open a second front in the Far East in order to make use of the German victory in the West.

00:39:36.738 --> 00:39:37.098
SORGA,

00:39:37.578 --> 00:39:42.843
report on the behavior of the Japanese government regarding the German war against the Soviet Union.

00:39:46.346 --> 00:39:50.109
OT is attempting to push Japan into war against the Soviet Union.

00:39:50.389 --> 00:39:52.010
according to military sources,

00:39:52.151 --> 00:39:53.992
possible within one or two months.

00:39:56.034 --> 00:39:59.917
Stalin's appreciation for Sorge has grown since June 22,

00:40:00.317 --> 00:40:02.599
but now Sorge feels like he is failing.

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:05.241
Japan's true intentions are unclear.

00:40:05.922 --> 00:40:10.345
An attack on Siberia can neither be ruled out nor predicted with certainty.

00:40:14.429 --> 00:40:17.091
The German armed forces are advancing into Russia,

00:40:17.391 --> 00:40:19.193
bringing the Red Army into distress.

00:40:19.533 --> 00:40:21.634
They need reinforcements from the Far East,

00:40:21.734 --> 00:40:24.454
but that would turn Siberia into a sitting duck.

00:40:27.855 --> 00:40:31.276
And then the master spy pulled off perhaps his biggest coup.

00:40:31.676 --> 00:40:32.857
After a secret meeting,

00:40:32.937 --> 00:40:34.597
which the emperor also attended,

00:40:34.777 --> 00:40:37.658
the salvific details seep out through Osaka,

00:40:37.878 --> 00:40:40.479
and Sorga immediately conveys them to Moscow.

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:46.501
Japan will not attack the Soviet Union in the east.

00:40:51.185 --> 00:41:00.431
Stalin immediately shifts 34 well-rested divisions from the Far East to the West and is able to stop the German armed forces as they rush ahead to Moscow.

00:41:00.811 --> 00:41:03.512
Sorge considers his mission in Japan to be over.

00:41:03.873 --> 00:41:05.153
He wants to leave the country,

00:41:05.474 --> 00:41:06.254
but where will he go?

00:41:10.537 --> 00:41:12.598
Sorge had thought about returning to Moscow,

00:41:13.218 --> 00:41:17.621
but a person as clever as him would certainly not assume that Moscow would be safe for him.

00:41:19.844 --> 00:41:24.607
He had surely considered the possibility that he would be arrested and killed in Moscow.

00:41:27.968 --> 00:41:28.729
Even in Japan,

00:41:29.169 --> 00:41:30.690
he would most likely be arrested.

00:41:31.530 --> 00:41:33.451
He could have also returned to Nazi Germany,

00:41:34.592 --> 00:41:37.674
but there would have been a high risk of being arrested by the Gestapo.

00:41:44.517 --> 00:41:47.039
Exile in the US would have also been a possibility.

00:41:47.587 --> 00:41:48.487
But as a communist,

00:41:48.967 --> 00:41:50.188
immigrating to the U.S.

00:41:50.368 --> 00:41:52.949
would have meant having to renounce his entire life.

00:41:58.150 --> 00:42:03.812
As Ozaki provides Zorgo with further details of secret talks between the Japanese and the Americans,

00:42:04.072 --> 00:42:07.894
neither one knows that the edges of their spy network have begun to fray,

00:42:08.374 --> 00:42:12.115
and that they themselves are now in the crosshairs of Japanese shadows.

00:42:18.396 --> 00:42:24.958
There was absolutely no clearly worked out plan for what to do if Sorge were to be arrested.

00:42:29.059 --> 00:42:34.041
That helps to explain why the entire ring was relatively quickly discovered and arrested in

00:42:35.582 --> 00:42:38.703
1941.

00:42:40.080 --> 00:42:47.706
Ozaki views the talks between Japan and the US as destined to fail because Japan will hold on to its policy of expansion.

00:42:50.728 --> 00:42:56.573
Sorge composes a dispatch in which he prophesizes the imminent war between Japan and the US.

00:42:56.993 --> 00:42:59.155
The message no longer reaches Moscow.

00:43:02.059 --> 00:43:03.700
It was likely an unimportant,

00:43:03.880 --> 00:43:04.801
low-level spy,

00:43:04.941 --> 00:43:11.245
a Japanese communist that had returned from the US who revealed Miyagi's name in order to save his own skin.

00:43:11.525 --> 00:43:12.246
As a result,

00:43:12.366 --> 00:43:13.847
the whole ring was busted.

00:43:14.928 --> 00:43:17.670
On October 15,

00:43:17.671 --> 00:43:18.570
1941,

00:43:18.571 --> 00:43:19.491
Ozaki Hatsumi is arrested.

00:43:37.653 --> 00:43:38.213
Klausen,

00:43:38.513 --> 00:43:41.474
Vukolic and Sorge meet on October 17.

00:43:42.194 --> 00:43:43.874
They are unable to reach Ozaki.

00:43:48.756 --> 00:43:52.577
Richard Sorge has been plagued by premonitions for quite some time.

00:43:53.057 --> 00:43:59.379
He felt abandoned by Moscow and knew that they were all playing with fire and could not remain undiscovered forever.

00:44:03.781 --> 00:44:05.762
We don't know when he came home that night,

00:44:07.183 --> 00:44:11.887
but on the following morning he was arrested by investigating magistrate Yoshikawa.

00:44:28.059 --> 00:44:29.300
Shortly before his arrest,

00:44:29.360 --> 00:44:31.982
he believed he had accomplished his mission in Tokyo.

00:44:32.382 --> 00:44:34.124
He had reported the most important things,

00:44:34.844 --> 00:44:36.505
the German attack on the Soviet Union,

00:44:36.886 --> 00:44:39.288
and that the Japanese would not attack the Soviet Union.

00:44:39.908 --> 00:44:46.733
And he had asked to be recalled because the last decade in which he had been a spy was so stressful that he simply needed peace and quiet.

00:44:47.974 --> 00:44:49.355
This dangerous document,

00:44:49.535 --> 00:44:52.597
the request to be recalled after fulfilling his mission,

00:44:52.857 --> 00:44:54.899
remains laying on Sorge's desk.

00:44:55.579 --> 00:44:57.820
Sorga is transferred to the Ruman prison,

00:44:57.920 --> 00:44:58.400
Sugamo.

00:44:59.200 --> 00:45:00.280
For Ambassador Ott,

00:45:00.580 --> 00:45:03.061
it is a case of Japanese spy hysteria.

00:45:08.543 --> 00:45:14.564
Members of the embassy and public authorities agree that the suspicion lodged against Sorga is far-fetched.

00:45:15.105 --> 00:45:19.566
There is suspicion that it is actually a case of political revenge or intrigue.

00:45:19.986 --> 00:45:20.186
Ott.

00:45:25.130 --> 00:45:26.934
When Sorge and Ozaki were arrested,

00:45:27.435 --> 00:45:29.520
the German government protested,

00:45:30.622 --> 00:45:32.366
or rather the German embassy in Japan.

00:45:33.448 --> 00:45:37.609
Asking how a trustworthy National Socialist like Sorge could be arrested.

00:45:41.710 --> 00:45:44.831
Japan could not afford to insult its Axis partner,

00:45:45.171 --> 00:45:46.332
especially not now,

00:45:46.552 --> 00:45:48.032
when the conflict with the U.S.

00:45:48.112 --> 00:45:49.533
appeared to be unavoidable.

00:45:52.814 --> 00:45:54.674
In spite of continuing efforts,

00:45:54.974 --> 00:46:00.616
the Foreign Ministry has thus far not presented any evidence of guilt against Sorge and Clausen.

00:46:02.836 --> 00:46:04.237
One week after his arrest,

00:46:04.457 --> 00:46:07.399
Richard Sorge admits to being a communist spy.

00:46:09.080 --> 00:46:13.844
Meisinger and Ott were coming under serious fire.

00:46:14.024 --> 00:46:16.425
They believed until the end that Sorge was their friend.

00:46:16.585 --> 00:46:17.226
On December 5,

00:46:17.227 --> 00:46:21.789
1941,

00:46:21.949 --> 00:46:24.851
the Red Army begins a counteroffensive near Moscow.

00:46:25.251 --> 00:46:26.552
The tables are turning.

00:46:30.835 --> 00:46:31.916
As he sat in jail,

00:46:32.276 --> 00:46:33.696
Zorga might have asked himself,

00:46:33.917 --> 00:46:39.638
what would have happened if I had completed my task of raising awareness about the Japanese-American crisis?

00:46:39.958 --> 00:46:43.740
Japan uses the oil embargo as a reason to attack the U.S.,

00:46:44.040 --> 00:46:45.280
drawing them into the war.

00:46:45.500 --> 00:46:47.641
Zorga's prophecy came true on December

00:46:48.041 --> 00:46:48.161
7th.

00:46:52.242 --> 00:46:54.783
Rebentrop requested Zorga's extradition.

00:46:55.903 --> 00:46:57.384
The Japanese refuse.

00:46:57.664 --> 00:47:03.068
The war has turned and Zorga could serve as a valuable bargaining chip in negotiations with Moscow.

00:47:05.430 --> 00:47:07.311
After five months of interrogation,

00:47:07.471 --> 00:47:11.854
the police officer Ohashi presents his final report to the state prosecutor.

00:47:12.355 --> 00:47:15.337
Zorga addresses him with personal remarks and thanks him.

00:47:16.578 --> 00:47:19.420
For the thorough and extremely friendly review of my case,

00:47:20.841 --> 00:47:25.364
I will never forget how friendly you were to me in the most difficult time of my eventful life.

00:47:28.340 --> 00:47:30.982
Ohashi's report recommends the death penalty.

00:47:39.069 --> 00:47:42.092
Richard Sorgas declared guilty and sentenced to death.

00:47:46.676 --> 00:47:49.398
He believes that Stalin will arrange for his rescue.

00:47:49.979 --> 00:47:52.901
If he had known about his wife Katya's life of suffering,

00:47:53.021 --> 00:47:55.623
he would not have given himself over to this illusion.

00:47:58.220 --> 00:48:00.042
Stalin's henchmen had arrested her,

00:48:00.442 --> 00:48:03.604
accused her of being a spy for the German secret services,

00:48:03.905 --> 00:48:05.946
sentenced her to banishment in Siberia,

00:48:06.227 --> 00:48:07.287
where she soon died.

00:48:09.189 --> 00:48:12.932
Her crime was being the wife of Richard Sorga.

00:48:19.057 --> 00:48:22.640
When the Japanese actually were ready to engage in a spy swap,

00:48:23.040 --> 00:48:23.981
Moscow claimed,

00:48:24.401 --> 00:48:26.883
The name Richard Sorga is unknown to us.

00:48:34.227 --> 00:48:40.931
Sorge went from being the betrayer to the betrayed.

00:48:41.011 --> 00:48:42.852
His contribution was invaluable.

00:48:44.133 --> 00:48:49.235
No other person had delivered so much information to us about Japan in this intense period.

00:48:51.577 --> 00:48:55.039
Sorge revealed Japan's situation and problems from A to Z.

00:48:56.059 --> 00:48:56.680
Fundamental.

00:48:57.600 --> 00:48:59.081
He was our most valuable worker.

00:49:03.764 --> 00:49:05.045
When he could no longer deliver,

00:49:05.425 --> 00:49:07.567
he was treated like a used-up resource.

00:49:08.107 --> 00:49:10.109
He wasn't interesting anymore.

00:49:11.290 --> 00:49:11.650
Anyway,

00:49:11.730 --> 00:49:14.572
it was known that he had talked openly with the investigators.

00:49:15.292 --> 00:49:18.515
That's why the Soviet government didn't put any effort into saving

00:49:21.577 --> 00:49:24.779
Zorga.

00:49:26.488 --> 00:49:29.429
Ozaki is also sentenced to death and executed.

00:49:31.549 --> 00:49:33.830
Max Clausen receives life imprisonment.

00:49:34.090 --> 00:49:38.051
He is freed in 1945.

00:49:38.091 --> 00:49:43.513
Branko Vukulic receives a life sentence and dies in prison in 1944.

00:49:43.514 --> 00:49:46.413
Miyagi dies in 1943 during the trial.

00:49:50.855 --> 00:49:55.416
Saga made it clear in his notes that he was as much against Hitler as he was against Stalin.

00:49:57.457 --> 00:49:58.518
And that as a communist,

00:49:58.778 --> 00:50:01.760
he assumed that the ideals of socialism and communism,

00:50:02.401 --> 00:50:03.662
not Stalin as a person,

00:50:04.062 --> 00:50:05.603
would be fulfilled in the end.

00:50:06.524 --> 00:50:08.546
After he had set these thoughts down on paper,

00:50:08.966 --> 00:50:09.366
he was,

00:50:09.406 --> 00:50:09.747
I think,

00:50:10.187 --> 00:50:10.867
ready for death.

00:50:13.750 --> 00:50:18.473
It remains unclear what the course of the war would have been without the Tokyo warnings.

00:50:19.174 --> 00:50:22.056
It also remains unclear if and to what extent

00:50:22.380 --> 00:50:27.787
Sorge became a double agent in the hope of gaining access to even more meaningful Nazi sources.

00:50:28.948 --> 00:50:31.331
Because he had witnessed hell in the trenches,

00:50:31.871 --> 00:50:32.212
Sorge,

00:50:32.392 --> 00:50:35.115
a man who actually never even wanted to be a spy,

00:50:35.516 --> 00:50:36.056
became

00:50:36.577 --> 00:50:38.099
Stalin's James Bond.

00:50:43.461 --> 00:50:50.964
One of Stalin's greatest mistakes was that he ignored Saga's information about the German invasion and was therefore not prepared.

00:50:52.345 --> 00:50:54.066
Saga was dangerous to him for that reason.

00:50:54.766 --> 00:50:56.387
He could have brought this mistake to light.

00:50:59.768 --> 00:50:59.988
Thus,

00:51:00.048 --> 00:51:00.648
for Stalin,

00:51:01.009 --> 00:51:04.090
it would have been extremely dangerous to bring Saga back to Moscow.

00:51:05.591 --> 00:51:06.291
On the contrary,

00:51:06.791 --> 00:51:10.773
it was advantageous that the Japanese kept Saga prisoner and executed him.

00:51:12.909 --> 00:51:15.951
That's why Stalin didn't take an interest in exchanging spies.

00:51:16.731 --> 00:51:18.853
When Sorge was executed on November 7th,

00:51:18.854 --> 00:51:20.333
1944,

00:51:20.814 --> 00:51:23.095
Stalin was perhaps more pleased than anyone.

00:51:23.215 --> 00:51:24.195
On November 7th,

00:51:24.196 --> 00:51:28.838
1944,

00:51:30.819 --> 00:51:32.020
disowned by everyone,

00:51:32.460 --> 00:51:34.161
Sorge goes to his execution.

00:51:41.517 --> 00:51:43.118
Long live international communism.

00:51:44.799 --> 00:51:45.239
Banzai.

00:51:48.481 --> 00:51:51.863
His last words defiantly repeat his unbroken faith.

00:51:55.105 --> 00:51:55.926
November 5th,

00:51:56.366 --> 00:51:58.467
1964.

00:51:58.487 --> 00:51:58.868
Richard Sorge,

00:51:58.869 --> 00:52:01.029
honored as a hero of the Soviet Union.

